   "body": "Adversarial review round 1 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\nAdversarial review (Fable 5.2): REQUEST CHANGES at 2f0343eb8e3a44b24272e8a485149d0af3181be3\n\nThe cell `055, 057` is correct and `lots.json` is exact. One tool still ignores the cell.\n\n1. **Medium** — `tooling/roadmap/render.py:14-15`. `special()` hardcodes LOT-070 as `⛔ waits on every engine lot (gate)`, whatever its state. Scenario: `render.py` on this head writes that text for LOT-070 in `post-mvp.md` (board #324), while `generate.state('LOT-070')` returns `⛔ waits on 055, 057`. The board contradicts the plan and the operator's decision, and would still say so once #94 is ready or claimed. Fix: delete `special()` and use `state(l)[1]`.\n2. **Low** — `tooling/roadmap/render.py:102`. `triage()` skips LOT-070 (`l!='LOT-070'`). Scenario: #81 and #83 close, #94 stays `status: blocked`; it is never listed for triage. Fix: drop the exclusion, now that the cell is numeric.\n3. **Low** — `tooling/roadmap/classify_blocked.py:71-72`. The note for #94 still says its section \"asks the operator whether LOT-168 and LOT-184 gate the engine parity\". Decided on 2026-11-12. Fix: cite the decision.\n4. **Detail** — `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md:36` gives \"all parsing/network/storage lots\" as an example gate cell; no cell holds a gate sentence any more. Reword, or say none is left.\n5. **Detail** — the body of #94 still reads `### Depends on (all parsing/network/storage lots)`. Outside the diff: update it after the merge.\n\n**Verified**\n- Tracker state of all 74 non-App lot rows (every HFRModels, HFRParsing, HFRNetwork, HFRStorage, HFRClient row): all closed as completed, except #81 (LOT-055), #83 (LOT-057), #286 (LOT-168), #449 (LOT-184) and #94 itself.\n- `lots_from_md.py` output is byte-identical to the committed `lots.json` (174 lots).\n- `hygiene.numeric_deps('055, 057')` returns both lots; `hygiene.py` dry run no longer treats #94 as a gate sentence; `unblocked.py` and `generate.deps` read the cell; `check-lot-deps.py`: 0 violations.\n- 177 tests of `scripts/tests` pass on the head and on the base files alike: no test covers this change.\n- `render.py` run offline (finding 1).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
