   "body": "Adversarial review round 2 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\nAdversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE at f0cbe8f9490513333c0e9384ef3998ed5ac03d2f\n\nRound 2. Findings 1 to 4 of round 1 are fixed; no new blocking finding.\n\n1. **Fixed** — `tooling/roadmap/render.py`: `special()` is gone. The rendered `post-mvp.md` now shows LOT-070 as `⛔ waits on 055, 057`, as `generate.state` returns it.\n2. **Fixed** — `tooling/roadmap/render.py:99`: `triage()` no longer skips LOT-070.\n3. **Fixed** — `tooling/roadmap/classify_blocked.py:71-72`: the note for #94 cites the decision of 2026-11-12.\n4. **Fixed** — `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md:36`: the gate-cell example says none is left. This is true: the only non-numeric cell left is LOT-034's `030, ADR 0006`, which is not a gate sentence and whose issue is closed.\n5. **Open, by agreement** — the body of #94 still reads `### Depends on (all parsing/network/storage lots)`; to update after the merge.\n6. **Detail, not blocking** — no test covers the `render.py` change: the 177 tests pass with and without it. `render.py` writes the boards on import, so the tests only read its source (`scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py:171`). A regression here would only be seen on the board.\n\n**Verified**\n- `git diff 2f0343eb..HEAD` and the whole PR (5 files, 7 insertions, 10 deletions).\n- No reference to `special(`, to the old gate text or to the LOT-070 exclusion is left in `tooling`, `scripts` or `docs`.\n- `lots_from_md.py` output is byte-identical to the committed `lots.json` (174 lots).\n- `render.py` runs offline with exit code 0; `classify_blocked.py` loads.\n- 177 tests of `scripts/tests` pass.\n- The branch merges cleanly into the current `origin/dev-swift`, which has no new commit since the branch point.\n- Round 1's tracker check stands: every engine lot is closed except #81, #83, #286 and #449.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
